A||N||7||FIERO1985||Most Power out of 2.8L||||4||
Z||000000||FIERO1985||12-19-2001||09:33 PM||||Alright, I have been in a constant battle between modding the 2.8 or doing a swap. I dont mind dropping the craddle. to rebuild my 2.8L. I have done it before to do clutch. I am just wondering whether all the money for a 5.7 is worth it? I would like to know what is a good number for max reached HP out of a 2.8L snd how it was done. Info on Turbos,Stroked,and bolt on motors are all helpful.<P>As always thanks for any help available,<BR>Dan<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||4
Z||000001||Fierokid87||12-19-2001||09:37 PM||||Id say doing the right stuff like exaust, porting exaust manifolds, and alot of performance engine work will get you to about 200 or a bit more.  Im rebuilding a 2.8 bored to a 2.9<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIERO1985||12-19-2001||09:53 PM||||Sounds good, but if you stroke to a 3.1 and do a turbo kit with some bolt ons (coldair, larger throttle body, injectors,underdrive pullys and headers and a full exhaust, plus maybe a little head work and thinks of that nature would set someone back oh say....2000 total being generous if all labor accept engine rebuild is done by myself would give me how much power? They say that on a stock 2.8L the turbo gives like 205 Hp at 9 psi? so 200 plus 10 for cold air, 10-12 for TB, pullys and exhaust 25 head work and valves and maybe a couple others around 35 hp so that it could be up and around 260-280 hp...Is that a good estimate or am I over or under. Tryin to see if actually modding out a 2.8L is worth the effort or just do Archies kit. But as I said is the 6-7K really the best bet as for as a engine mod SBC or invest 3K and have a tricked out 2.8L and still do some exterior and interior mods&gt; Just want to get a little info,<P>Thank you for any info as always.<P>Dan<BR>85gt<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||2
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||12-19-2001||11:49 PM||||I'm afraid that your HP estimates are a bit off. You won't get as much HP from each of the mods that you listed above. For instance:<BR>the bored out t-body will provide about a 5 HP gain, maybe 7 with a matching intake. I<BR>can tell you that you're very unlikely to find 25 HP from head porting too. The stock heads flow pretty good but would benefit from<BR>a multi angle valve job and some bowl porting but those mods certainly won't give you anywhere near 25 HP. I have built a 3.2<BR>V6 in my GT with a lot of the stuff you listed above and even custom 10:1 forged pistons and I can tell you that the engine is<BR>pretty quick, so the V6 is worth building if you do it right BUT with a Chevy small block<BR>you can have pretty much however much power you want! In the end it really comes down to what you want to do and what's right for you.<BR>If you've got the money and a good place to do the swap then with the V8 you'll have a real monster. If you feel more comfortable doing a V6 which wouldn't require as much work then go for that but remember that if<BR>you build the V6 then take the time to really get into it. Don't expect a handful of bolt on parts to make you the fastest car on the road because it won't! Also: take the time to break the car in correctly and install some safety items like a high vol oil pump, maybe an oil cooler, some ARP bolts,etc.<BR>Whew, sorry for the length of that post.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>Activities Director<BR>Northern IL. Fiero Enthusiasts<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000004||88VortechGT||12-20-2001||11:00 AM||||Check out the post about my supercharger set-up in the technical forum to see what kind of potential you can get out of a 2.8. Now my engine cost me about$12,000 to build but it will be a fun ride when it's back in the car, and oh it crank dynoed at 35O HP, but the only thing about the engine is it's not a 2.8 anymore since it's been stroked to a 3.1 and overbored to a 3.3. I will be posting the dyno graphs after the holidays, I have to scan them in and email them to some body else to post for me since I am on a Macintosh G4<p>[This message has been edited by 88VortechGT (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||12-20-2001||12:44 PM||||I'd have to agree... you're estimates are padded a bit too much. I've got a mild-built 3.1 (3.2) with Port & Polished heads, ported exhaust, bored-out TB & Intake, and slightly decked heads.  There is definitely quite a difference over a stock 2.8, or even a stock 3.1L.  But even guesstimating mine at 200hp is optimistic.  If you want for alot more power- then you really need to go with some sort of unnatural aspiration (Turbo, Supercharger, Nitrous).<P>Although I do quite enjoy my 3.1L,  I am working on acquiring an LT1 to drop in at a later date.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||chester||12-21-2001||09:55 AM||||I know a guy that pushes 425HP out of a 2.8 with a T4 turbo.  The motor has the potential but it gets expensive.  I have about 3700 in my motor not counting programmable ECM turbo or NOS.  By the time I'm totally done I'm grasping for 300HP.  I'll probably have 5000-6000 in the motor by the time I'm done.  Could have done a V8 swap for the same money but the shock value is not the same when you whoop someone and open the decklid to reveal a 6  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> .<P>Rob D.<P><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">       <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000007||lou_dias||12-21-2001||02:24 PM||||my original 3.4 dynoed at 147 hp with a restrictive SpiralMax infront of the TB and 203 ft*lbs of torque.  It was overbored, I don't know how much.  I blew the engine last March.  I'm in the process of putting in a used 3.4...Should be done by New Year's<P>I had poorly ported heads (I mean poorly), K&N, and IRM dual exhaust (not cat, no muffler), Crane Compucam .423/.423", 1.52 roller rockers<P>New mods also include bored out TB and intake, real ported and polished heads, polished valves and stock Camaro cam which is better for peak hp and I am going to block of the EGR (which has done wonders for my 2.8 88 GT).<P>I will dyno it a week or 2 after it is done.<P>I expect to see 160hp at the wheels and the same torque.||||reg||1
